## Prerequisites

- Docker and Docker Compose (v2 plugin: `docker compose`, or classic `docker-compose`)
- Git
- Python **3.10+** for local development (3.12 is common on Ubuntu 24.04–based images)
- Maven (handled automatically in Dockerfile)
- **For ReAct Agents / Cloudera**: `openai>=1.0.0`, optional `python-dotenv` for repo `.env` (see `.env.example`)

### Docker image notes

- **`PYTHONPATH`**: The image sets Flink Agents **and** embedded PyFlink (`pyflink.zip` + `py4j-src.zip` under `/opt/flink/opt/python/`) so `import flink_agents` and `import pyflink` work from **`python3`** without activating the `uv` venv. The Flink Agents tree itself lives at **`/opt/flink/pythonpath/agent-site-packages`** (symlink into the `uv` virtualenv).
- **Compose sidecars** (`dashboard`, `log-processor` in `docker-compose-cowrie.yml`): On PEP 668–managed Python, installs use `python3 -m pip install --break-system-packages ...`. After pulling newer compose YAML, recreate services:  
  `docker compose -f docker-compose-cowrie.yml up -d --force-recreate dashboard log-processor`

## Flink Agents Version

This project defaults to **Apache Flink Agents v0.3-SNAPSHOT** (built from the [`apache/flink-agents`](https://github.com/apache/flink-agents) `main` branch). APIs and docs follow the **[Flink Agents 0.3 documentation](https://nightlies.apache.org/flink/flink-agents-docs-release-0.3/)** (preview; 0.3.0 is not yet tagged).

The Docker image uses **Apache Flink 2.2.0** (Flink Agents 0.3 requires Flink 1.20.3+).

To use a different git ref, set the build argument:

```bash
# Default: main → v0.3-SNAPSHOT
flink-cowrie build

# Latest stable tagged release (0.2.1)
flink-cowrie build release-0.2.1
docker build --build-arg FLINK_AGENTS_VERSION=release-0.2.1 -t agent_flink_image:0.2.1 .
```

See [VERSION.md](VERSION.md) and [docs/FLINK_AGENTS_VERSION.md](docs/FLINK_AGENTS_VERSION.md) for the full version matrix and import paths.

## 🔍 How Flink Agents Enhance Security Operations

### Traditional SIEM vs. Flink Agents

| Traditional SIEM | Flink Agents |
|------------------|--------------|
| Batch processing (minutes/hours delay) | Real-time streaming (milliseconds) |
| Rule-based detection | AI-powered intelligent analysis |
| Manual response actions | Automated response workflows |
| Limited context awareness | Stateful tracking across time windows |
| Static correlation rules | Dynamic pattern recognition |

### Real-Time Threat Detection Pipeline

```text
Internet Attacks → Cowrie Honeypot → Flink Agents → Automated Response
                                              ↓
                                    ┌─────────┴─────────┐
                                    │                   │
                            Threat Analysis      Response Actions
                                    │                   │
                    ┌───────────────┼───────────────┐  │
                    │               │               │  │
              Pattern      IP Reputation    Command    │
            Detection         Check        Analysis    │
                    │               │               │  │
                    └───────────────┼───────────────┘  │
                                    │                   │
                            ┌───────┴────────┐         │
                            │                │         │
                    Alert Generation    Action Execution
                            │                │         │
                    ┌───────┴───────┐  ┌────┴─────┐  │
                    │               │  │          │  │
                Dashboard    Slack/Email  Block IP  Threat Intel
```

