## 🔧 Troubleshooting

### Issue: Cowrie not capturing attacks
```bash
# Check if Cowrie is running
docker compose -f docker-compose-cowrie.yml ps

# Check Cowrie logs
docker compose -f docker-compose-cowrie.yml logs cowrie

# Verify ports are exposed
lsof -i :2222  # SSH port
lsof -i :2223  # Telnet port

# Check firewall rules (if running on cloud)
```

### Issue: Flink Agents not processing logs
```bash
# Check log processor service
docker compose -f docker-compose-cowrie.yml logs log-processor

# Verify Flink Agents installation
docker exec -it flinkdockerwithagents-taskmanager-1 bash -c \
  "export PYTHONPATH=/opt/flink/pythonpath/agent-site-packages:/opt/flink/opt/python/pyflink.zip:/opt/flink/opt/python/py4j-src.zip && python3 -c 'import flink_agents'"

# Check log file permissions
ls -la cowrie-logs/
```

### Issue: Dashboard not updating
```bash
# Check dashboard service
docker compose -f docker-compose-cowrie.yml logs dashboard

# Verify dashboard data file exists
ls -la cowrie-dashboard-data.json

# Check dashboard URL
curl http://localhost:8501
```

### Issue: Dashboard or log-processor keeps restarting (PEP 668)

If logs show **`externally-managed-environment`**, the container is still using an old **`command:`** that ran plain `pip3 install`. Current compose files use **`python3 -m pip install --break-system-packages ...`**. Pull the latest `docker-compose-cowrie.yml` and recreate:

```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose-cowrie.yml up -d --force-recreate dashboard log-processor
```

### Issue: Module not found
- Ensure flink-agents is installed in the container
- Check that the Dockerfile successfully built: `docker images | grep agent_flink_image`
- Rebuild if needed: `./deployScript.sh`

### Issue: Job fails to start
- Check Flink Web UI for error messages: http://localhost:8081
- For the cluster launch smoke test, see [test/README.md](test/README.md) (cluster troubleshooting table)
- Verify container logs: `docker compose -f docker-compose-cowrie.yml logs`
- Check resource limits (memory, CPU)

### Issue: No jobs in Flink Web UI after `test launch --cluster`
- Jobs only appear when submitted via **`flink run`** on the compose JobManager, not when using the Flink Agents local runner alone
- Run `flink-cowrie test launch --cluster --in-container` (starts minimal stack if needed)
- Ensure TaskManager can resolve `jobmanager` (restart stack: `flink-cowrie down && flink-cowrie up --profile minimal`)
- Check completed jobs: http://localhost:8081/#/job/completed

